{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>This is the book of the generations of Adam.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, explains that it alludes to the entire Torah, for the entire Torah is a book of the generations of Adam. For were it not so, why did it say 'book'? It should have said 'אלה תולדות אדם' — 'these are the generations of Adam' — in the manner of (Genesis 25:12) 'ואלה תולדות ישמעאל'; (Genesis 25:19) 'ואלה תולדות יצחק' — end of quotation. And it is possible to say regarding the word 'ספר' (book) that it is wisdom, from the root of 'ספר' and 'ספור' (telling) mentioned in the Sefer Yetzirah, which are names for the supernal wisdom. And Scripture declares, 'זה ספר' — 'this is the book' — that wisdom was worthy of being the generations of man, for the sons of physical man are not his essential progeny; rather, the book of wisdom is, for it is possible for the world to be sustained through others, as Ben Azzai said: 'What shall I do, for my soul cleaves to the Torah? It is possible for the world to be sustained through others.' And Scripture further explains that this book, which is wisdom, is fitting to be ascribed to man because 'בדמות אלהים עשה אותו' — 'in the likeness of Elohim He made him.' And when did He make him? 'ביום ברא אלהים אדם' — 'on the day that Elohim created Adam.' And understand this: why it was necessary to mention 'Adam' two times."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:31.148636471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}